## Version-premise corrections (verified during build)
  - The 2.2.21 RELEASE is NOT CVE-2011-3368-patched: the fix (trunk r1179239) was committed 2011-10-05,
    AFTER 2.2.21's release (2011-09-13). 2.2.21 ships only a dangling ap_proxy_request_status declaration.
  - The CVE-2011-3639-specific HTTP/0.9 `@`-URI vector does NOT reproduce on the 2.2.x codebase: verified
    that 2.2.21 gates request dispatch on r->status==HTTP_OK, so a 400 set for a bad request-URI blocks BOTH
    HTTP/1.0 and HTTP/0.9. That 0.9 bug was specific to the trunk r1179239 protocol.c approach, which the
    2.2 release lineage never shipped. The reproducible incomplete-fix on 2.2.x is the sibling-front-end
    residual above (the shared "additional reverse-proxy cases" issue tracked as both CVE-2011-3639 and
    CVE-2011-4317; sibling case: apache-http-server-mod-proxy-cve-2011-4317).

